    <h1>Terms &amp; Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Last updated: May 2026</p>

    <h2>Not Financial or Insurance Advice</h2>
    <p>
      All content on Was Pet Insurance Worth It is provided for educational and informational
      purposes only. Nothing on this site constitutes financial advice, insurance advice, or a
      recommendation to purchase or decline any insurance product. The calculator provides general
      estimates to help you think through the decision — it is not a substitute for professional
      financial guidance.
    </p>

    <h2>Results Are Estimates</h2>
    <p>
      All calculator outputs are retrospective estimates based on population-level data from 50,000
      pets and 210,000 claims. Your individual experience will vary based on your pet's actual
      health events, your specific policy terms, your insurer's reimbursement practices, and factors
      not captured by this tool. The calculator uses industry-average premiums from NAPHIA — your
      actual premium may be higher or lower.
    </p>

    <h2>Policy Assumptions</h2>
    <p>
      Unless otherwise stated, calculations assume: $500 annual deductible, 80% reimbursement rate,
      $15,000 annual limit, accident and illness coverage only (no wellness rider). Your actual
      policy terms may differ significantly.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Sources</h2>
    <p>
      Primary dataset: 50,000 pets, 210,235 claims (2018–2020), from a publicly available research
      dataset. Industry baselines from the NAPHIA 2024 State of the Industry Report. Breed-specific
      claim frequencies are derived from published veterinary research. We make no guarantee that
      the data is complete, current, or representative of your specific pet or insurer.
    </p>

    <h2>No Affiliations</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by any pet insurance company,
      veterinary organization, or financial institution. We do not sell insurance policies and
